<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Jan-June vehicle output up, exports down.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Jan-June vehicle output up, exports down.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's automobile industry produced 636,812 vehicles during the first six months of the year versus the same period in 1996, a rise of 3.7 percent, the Mexican Automobile Industry Association (AMIA) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Mexico's vehicle exports fell 3.3 percent from the year-ago period, to 487,052 units during the year's first six months.  </p>
<p>National sales in the January-June period reached 194,592 units, an increase of 38.1 percent from the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>The following table compares production and sales data for cars and trucks and buses during the relevant periods.</p>
<p>				     JAN-JUNE 97	  JAN-JUNE 96</p>
<p>    TOTAL PRODUCTION	     636,812		 613,793</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	 158,884		 106,488</p>
<p>		 autos		 112,531		  70,247</p>
<p>		 trucks and buses   46,353		  36,241</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   477,928		 507,305</p>
<p>    DOMESTIC SALES		 194,592		 140,901</p>
<p>    TOTAL EXPORTS		  487,052		 503,567</p>
<p>		 autos		 297,550		 338,698</p>
<p>		 trucks and buses  189,502		 164,869</p>
<p>    DOMESTIC RETAIL SALES	193,227		 136,280</p>
<p>((-- Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
